If a patient meets at least 2 opioid-use-disorder-criteria and meets at most 3 opioid-use-disorder-criteria then the patient has a mild-opioid-use-disorder.
If a patient meets at least 4 opioid-use-disorder-criteria and meets at most 5 opioid-use-disorder-criteria then the patient has a moderate-opioid-use-disorder.
If a patient meets at least 6 opioid-use-disorder-criteria then the patient has a severe-opioid-use-disorder.
